==English==

===Etymology===
From {{der|en|fr|grandiose}}, from {{der|en|it|grandioso}}, from {{der|en|la|grandis|t=great, grand}} ({{cog|en|grand}}).

===Pronunciation===
* {{rhymes|en|əʊs}}

===Adjective===
{{en-adj}}

# [[large]] and [[impressive]], in [[size]], [[scope]] or [[extent]]
#* '''2019''', Nalini Mohabir, ''[https://www.theguardian.com/commentisfree/2019/mar/06/renaming-cook-islands-independence-maori Renaming the Cook Islands would be a vital step towards true independence]'' in the Guardian.
#*: Independence does not need to be a '''grandiose''' process of disconnection and severing ties.
# [[pompous]] or [[pretentious]]

